  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the claim direction, so positive signed values support the stated claim and negative signed values indicate the opposite association. The most important new discovery is H19: feature_037=1 versus feature_037=0 has a signed dependency-increasing contrast of +0.833 units with 95% interval +0.767 to +0.899 (R21). The interval lies far above the 0.15-unit threshold, so within this dataset I accept a large and precise association between feature_037 and stronger composite dependency. This is not a causal or generalizable claim; it may reflect correlation with other measured predictors or dataset construction. The feature_017 H17 result is also informative but in the opposite direction from its stated claim: the signed estimate is -0.423 with interval -0.520 to -0.327 (R20), meaning the raw contrast is large and positive, i.e., feature_010=1 is associated with weaker dependency. I reject the original H17 claim and register a reversed feature_010 claim with direction +1. Because the original analysis already establishes the raw contrast precisely and far beyond the threshold, I give the reversed claim initial status accept, linked to H17 with R20 as motivating evidence. I also propose two follow-up subgroup analyses for feature_037 at low and high feature_036 to see whether the large feature_037 association is consistent across the research-signature scale. These are dataset-internal association checks, not conditioning-based causal estimates, and the controller will enforce the cell-count rule.\n\nThe follow-up of the feature_058-by-feature_036 hypothesis is now more specific. H11, the direct feature_058 contrast in feature_036 <= -1, has a point estimate of +0.156, slightly above the threshold, but its interval +0.012 to +0.300 includes values far below the threshold (R12). H12 in feature_036 <= -0.5 is smaller and imprecise, with upper bound still above threshold (R11). H24 in the broader low-signature stratum feature_036 <= 0 is precise and null in the claimed direction (R15 upper bound 0.144), and H25 shows no high-signature reverse effect (R16 upper bound 0.130). Thus the evidence suggests a tail-specific rather than gradient-like signal if it is real. H11 remains unresolved and active because its point estimate crosses the threshold but uncertainty and subgroup-selection risk are material; I request independent validation for H11 rather than H19 or H17, because H19/H17 have intervals far from the decision boundary while H11 is threshold- and selection-sensitive. H13 and H14 do not support feature_007 or feature_015 as drivers of the low-feature_036 signal; H14 is closed, and H13 is deferred as a weak specificity check. H23 shows a precise null direct feature_007 contrast within feature_058=0 (upper bound 0.110), so I close H23 and also close H4: the marker-marker interaction line is not supported by an absolute stratum contrast. The broad screens produce a near-threshold feature_003 effect (R18 point 0.141, interval 0.062 to 0.220), which remains active but unresolved; feature_001 and feature_035 are precise nulls and closed. Competing explanations include true predictor associations in this dataset, correlated predictors sharing latent outcome structure, chance subgroup selection in the feature_036 tail, and multiple testing; the proposed validation and follow-ups are intended to separate these.",
  "research_notes": "Updated evidence state: accepted H19 (feature_037 strong dependency-increasing association) and registered reversed feature_010 claim with initial accept based on refuted H17. Original H17 rejected/closed because its large effect is opposite the claimed direction. H15 feature_003 is near threshold but uncertain; active. H11 is the key active tail hypothesis: point 0.156 above threshold but lower CI 0.012, so validation requested for H11. Low feature_036 line is now tail-specific: H24 <=0 precise null, H25 high reverse precise null, H12 <= -0.5 unresolved but broader; H13 specificity weak/deferred. Marker-marker line closed: H23 direct feature_007 in feature_058=0 is precise null, so H4 closed. H16/H26/H14 closed. Validation policy: validate H11 first because H19/H17 are far from threshold and validating them would be less informative. If validation supports H11 above threshold, consider accepting H11 and possibly the parent H7 interaction; if validation does not support threshold, close H11/H7/H12/H13 and stop tail-selection follow-up unless a direct non-tail signal emerges. After validation resolves, next analysis priorities are the feature_037 feature_036 subgroup follow-ups and H15/H12 if still credible. Avoid overfishing feature_036 cutoffs; keep H13 and broader low strata deferred. All accepted statements are dataset-internal associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
